    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "43359aaa_1640cf86",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 726,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-27T16:18:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This function does a lot of semi-related things. It checks a condition, maybe sets context-specific failure indicators, and maybe sets a flag affecting future state machine operation. It\u0027s hard to describe concisely.\n\nI would prefer that it be separated. VDM-specific actions should be in VDM-specific states. It looks to me like there are 3 cases that a VDM entry function has to deal with uniquely: already VCONN Source, not VCONN Source and able to request swap, and not VCONN Source and not able to request swap. The latter two require a state change. How about something like this?\n\n/* pe_vdm_send_request_entry */\nif (!tc_is_vconn_src(port)) {\n    if (try_become_vconn_src(port)) {\n        return;\n    }\n}\n\n/* VDM child state entry functions */\nif (!tc_is_vconn_src(port)) {\n    /* VDM-specific failure call */\n    set_state_pe(port, previous state);\n    return;\n}\n\n/* This should have a better name */\nvoid try_become_vconn_src(port) {\n    if (vconn_swap_counter \u003c N_VCONN_SWAP_COUNT) {\n        ++vconn_swap_counter;\n        PE_SET_FLAG(VCONN_SWAP_TO_ON);\n        set_state_pe(port, previous_state);\n        /* Returns true if state changed, false otherwise */\n        return true;\n    }\n    return false;\n}",
      "revId": "306a1f95783ed26f8a92b32bd2eaee8f37d3679a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b0a3b5ee_e20b964b",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 726,
      "author": {
        "id": 1329040
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-27T20:05:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So with this change, only for entry mode, we are trying VCONN swap 3 times. In other Discover VDMs, if we are not the VCONN src, we just do a VDM-specific failure?",
      "parentUuid": "43359aaa_1640cf86",
      "revId": "306a1f95783ed26f8a92b32bd2eaee8f37d3679a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "29a44b81_d30a5cbe",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 726,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-28T18:01:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "All of the VDM request states have PE_VDM_SEND_REQUEST as their parent, so they will all do the \"3 tries\" logic. The failure logic won\u0027t be executed unless the 3 tries have already been exhausted.",
      "parentUuid": "b0a3b5ee_e20b964b",
      "revId": "306a1f95783ed26f8a92b32bd2eaee8f37d3679a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
